the interest of his brother and village, making him remain a loyal shinobi of Konohagakure to the very end.	https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Itachi_Uchiha
Roy Mustang	{https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/fma/images/5/5b/MustangManga.png/revision/latest?cb=20250220111436,https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/fma/images/a/a8/Avatar_roy2003.png/revision/latest?cb=20171026204538,https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/fma/images/b/bb/Avatar_roy.png/revision/latest?cb=20171026195109,https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/fma/images/1/1e/Mustang_Full_Body.png/revision/latest?cb=20250220112246,https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/fma/images/a/a7/Royai0.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/1000?cb=20130417190530,https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/fma/images/c/c2/Roy_Mustang_using_flame_alchamy.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20090515141959,https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/fma/images/f/fe/Brotherhood53.jpg/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/1000?cb=20100419023403,https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/fma/images/9/90/Chapter34.jpg/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/1000?cb=20100408134336,...}	Full Metal Alchemist	39	Colonel Roy Mustang, the "Flame Alchemist", is a charismatic and ambitious State Alchemist within the Amestrian military, and a pivotal supporting character in Fullmetal Alchemist. Renowned for his powerful and versatile flame alchemy, which he activates using transmutation circles embroidered on special gloves that ignite the oxygen in the air, Mustang is both a respected officer and a ruthless strategist. Unlike many of his peers, his ambition is not simply to serve the state but to rise to the position of F├╝hrer (military dictator) of Amestris, motivated by a desire to reform the corrupt and rigid military structure and protect the people from the horrors of war.	https://fma.fandom.com/wiki/Roy_Mustang
Van Hohenheim	{https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/fma/images/a/ae/Hohenheim09.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width/360?cb=20180406215022,https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/fma/images/5/50/HohenheimManga.png/revision/latest?cb=20250220140417,https://cdn.staticneo.com/w/fullmetalalchemist/VanHohenheim.jpg,https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/fma/images/4/4c/Hohenheim03.png/revision/latest?cb=20130422231443,https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/fma/images/4/45/Souls.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/1000?cb=20130816005514,https://beneaththetangles.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/01/fma-2b.jpg,https://i0.wp.com/drunkenanimeblog.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/06/dvd-anime-full-metal-alchemist-brotherhood-dub-completo-d_nq_np_644905-mlb25106676244_102016-f.jpg?resize=640%2C399&ssl=1}	Full Metal Alchemist	40	Van Hohenheim ΓÇö known in the 2003 anime series as Hohenheim of Light and sometimes given the full name Hohenheim Elric or Van Hohenheim ElricΓÇöwas a deceptively ancient and extremely powerful Alchemist as well as the estranged father of Edward and Alphonse Elric. Despite disappearing suddenly during their infancy, Hohenheim returned during the course of the series in order to right the wrongs of his mysterious past.	https://fma.fandom.com/wiki/Van_Hohenheim
Erwin Smith	{https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/shingekinokyojin/images/d/de/Erwin_Smith_%28Anime%29_character_image.png/revision/latest?cb=20190604212647,https://static0.cbrimages.com/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2019/09/Attack-On-Titan-10-Things-You-Didnt-Know-About-Erwin-Smith-featured-image.jpg?w=1600&h=900&fit=crop,https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/shingekinokyojin/images/1/18/Erwin_Smith_character_image.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/1000?cb=20190514212751,https://encrypted-tbn0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcSNF6gg0Ma5hvCIRXdathHo1cqBaiOOBFOU7Q&s,https://wallpapers.com/images/featured/erwin-smith-5h3po771e9fa9c7q.jpg,https://miro.medium.com/v2/0*lWxW4GGasInhGZoO,https://static0.srcdn.com/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/AttackOnTitan-ErwinsMistakes-FeatureImage.jpeg?w=1200&h=628&fit=crop,https://i.pinimg.com/736x/92/6a/7a/926a7a24fea108e0c5e5bbcdd5ce0e25.jpg}	Attack on Titan	51	Erwin Smith is the 13th Commander of the Survey Corps in the Attack on Titan series, widely regarded as a brilliant military strategist and a master of psychological warfare. A man of imposing presence and unwavering resolve, he is best known for his "Long-Distance Enemy Scouting Formation," a tactic that significantly reduced casualty rates during expeditions beyond the Walls. ErwinΓÇÖs leadership is defined by a cold, calculated utilitarianism; he possesses a "nerves of steel" temperament that allows him to make agonizing sacrifices for the sake of humanity's survival. Whether leading a desperate charge against the Beast Titan or orchestrating a coup d'├⌐tat to overthrow a corrupt monarchy, Erwin operates with a level-headedness that inspires absolute, if sometimes fearful, loyalty from his subordinates.\n\nBeneath his stoic facade as humanityΓÇÖs "hope," Erwin is a deeply complex man haunted by a personal quest for the truth. His primary motivation stems from his childhood, where his curiosity about the world outside the Walls led to the death of his father, a history teacher. This tragedy instilled in him a lifelong obsession with proving his fatherΓÇÖs theories correct and discovering the true history of the world. Throughout his career, he struggled with the guilt of leading countless soldiers to their deaths to further his own "selfish" dream of reaching the basement of the Jaeger family home. Ultimately, ErwinΓÇÖs arc reaches a poignant conclusion when he chooses to abandon his personal desires, leading a suicidal charge to secure a future for the survivorsΓÇöa final act that solidified his legacy as one of the most respected, yet morally ambiguous, figures in military history.	https://attackontitan.fandom.com/wiki/Erwin_Smith
Spike Spiegel	{https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/cowboybebop/images/b/b2/Spike_Spiegel_Main.png/revision/latest?cb=20250315014957,https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f6/Spike_Spiegel_as_drawn_by_the_creators.jpg,https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/disneythehunchbackofnotredame/images/0/00/Screen_Shot_2013-12-11_at_12_52_29_PM.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/294?cb=20200415000005,https://static0.srcdn.com/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Cowboy-bebop-is-spike-spiegel-jewish-in-the-anime.jpg,https://static0.gamerantimages.com/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/Cowboy-Bebop-Anime-Sc-Fi.jpg?q=50&fit=crop&w=825&dpr=1.5,https://dotandline.net/wp-content/uploads/2018/04/1_58uZVuKlz4bhBJF1BL9qdA-1210x642.jpeg,"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!WbJA!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F1b9a65d9-ac85-4dc8-a159-a1a60a6be494_780x438.jpeg"}	Cowboy Bebop	59	Spike Spiegel is the cool and nonchalant protagonist of Cowboy Bebop, a bounty hunterΓÇöor "cowboy"ΓÇödrifting through the solar system in the year 2071 aboard the spaceship Bebop. A former hitman for the Red Dragon Crime Syndicate, Spike left his life of crime by faking his death after falling in love with a woman named Julia. This past remains a heavy burden, as he is constantly pursued by his former partner-turned-nemesis, Vicious. Spike lives by a fatalistic and detached philosophy, famously stating, "Whatever happens, happens," and often describes his existence as a "bad dream" from which he cannot wake up. His physical appearance is marked by his "uncool" green hair, a constant cigarette, and a cybernetic right eye that he claims "sees the present," while his natural left eye "sees the past."\n\nA master of Jeet Kune Do and a gifted pilot of his personal red racer, the Swordfish II, Spike is a formidable fighter who relies on fluid movements and exceptional hand-eye coordination. Despite his cynical exterior and his vocal dislike for "kids, animals, and women with attitudes," he develops a familial, albeit dysfunctional, bond with his crewmates: the former investigator Jet Black, the amnesiac gambler Faye Valentine, the eccentric hacker Ed, and the "data dog" Ein. His journey is defined by the tension between his desire for a peaceful future and the inescapable pull of his history. Ultimately, SpikeΓÇÖs story is a tragic exploration of a man unable to outrun his ghosts, culminating in a final, inevitable confrontation with the Syndicate to settle his debts once and for all.	https://cowboybebop.fandom.com/wiki/Spike_Spiegel
Arataka Reigen	{https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/mob-psycho-100/images/3/34/Reigen_Fullbody.png/revision/latest?cb=20220513110837,https://i.redd.it/is-that-reigen-arataka-from-hit-series-mob-psycho-100-v0-as3cwx4i5jfe1.jpg?width=735&format=pjpg&auto=webp&s=aa1d76dbe30451a7d2ec5d08aa62f0963e164b5a,https://static0.cbrimages.com/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/Mob-Psycho-100-Reigen-Arataka.jpg,https://i0.wp.com/wavemotioncannon.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/mob-psycho-ep11-16.jpg?fit=1200%2C675&ssl=1,https://static0.cbrimages.com/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/Mob-Psycho-100-Reigen-Arataka.jpg,https://encrypted-tbn0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTRR9-2dH1VYWghpO2G-booqp1xVzYcqbUeRg&s,https://m.media-amazon.com/images/M/MV5BYjUyNjEwNWYtNjFhMy00YzJhLTkyZDQtMjQ5NmMxOTUwY2Y3XkEyXkFqcGc@._V1_.jpg}	Mob Psycho 100	52	Arataka Reigen is the self-proclaimed "Greatest Psychic of the 21st Century" and the owner of the Spirits and Such Consultation Office in the series Mob Psycho 100. Despite his grand claims, Reigen is a mundane human with absolutely no psychic abilities, operating as a charismatic con artist who uses a combination of social engineering, parlor tricks, and "Special Techniques" like the Salt Splash or Graphic Exorcism to solve his clients' problems. His life took a pivotal turn when he met Shigeo "Mob" Kageyama, a young boy with immense psychic power; recognizing the boy's vulnerability, Reigen hired him as an assistant for a meager wage, using MobΓÇÖs actual powers to handle legitimate supernatural threats while posing as the mastermind behind the exorcisms.\n\nDespite his deceptive career, Reigen serves as an essential moral compass for Mob, instilling in him the belief that having special powers doesn't make one "less human" or inherently superior to others. His mentorship is defined by a deep, genuine care for MobΓÇÖs well-being, often putting himself in physical danger or sacrificing his own reputation to protect the boy's innocence. While he begins the series as a seemingly shallow opportunist, Reigen undergoes significant character development, eventually confronting his own loneliness and the ethics of his deception. By the end of his journey, he transitions from a manipulative boss to a true father figure and friend, proving that his greatest strength is not supernatural at all, but his profound empathy and common sense.	https://mob-psycho-100.fandom.com/wiki/Arataka_Reigen
Shigeo Kageyama	{https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/mob-psycho-100/images/b/b7/Mob_Fullbody.png/revision/latest?cb=20220513153327,https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/characterprofile/images/2/2d/Shigeo_Kageyama%2C_the_Strongest_Esper_of_Salt_Middle.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/250?cb=20160908202348,https://i.pinimg.com/736x/15/3e/59/153e591dec5803554c33c35e5016f35b.jpg,https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/characterprofile/images/3/34/100%25Mob.jpg/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/300?cb=20160908202406,https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/characterprofile/images/4/4f/---%25Mob.png/revision/latest?cb=20160908202416,https://a.storyblok.com/f/178900/640x360/e267b88a6d/b7fd57a2a56d7fda7e9da67645b18ac11550008892_full.png/m/640x360,https://a.storyblok.com/f/178900/640x359/9ee164391f/ab9a01b7d9fca84d118aad9ea97991d01550006691_full.png/m/640x359,https://a.storyblok.com/f/178900/640x360/3e17d70876/03aed3836623684528e20ddb3107f25c1550069381_full.png/m/640x360}	Mob Psycho 100	53	Shigeo Kageyama, affectionately known as "Mob," is the unassuming protagonist of Mob Psycho 100 and a middle school student with god-like psychic abilities. Despite being one of the world's most powerful espers, Mob is characterized by his profound humility and his desire to lead a completely normal life. Having accidentally hurt his younger brother, Ritsu, with his powers as a child, Shigeo developed a deep-seated fear of his own potential for destruction. To prevent his abilities from spiraling out of control, he subconsciously suppresses his emotions behind a stoic, expressionless mask. He lives by the philosophyΓÇötaught to him by his mentor, Arataka ReigenΓÇöthat psychic powers do not make one inherently superior to others, leading him to prioritize self-improvement in other areas, such as joining the Body Improvement Club to gain physical strength and social confidence.\n\nWhile Mob is typically gentle and non-confrontational, his suppressed feelings are tracked by an internal "counter" that progresses toward an explosion. When this counter reaches 100%, Mob is overwhelmed by a specific, intense emotionΓÇösuch as anger, sadness, or courageΓÇöreleasing a massive surge of psychic energy that allows him to reshape matter, fly, and erect impenetrable barriers. Beyond this lies the mysterious "???%" state, an unconscious level of power that triggers only when Mob is physically incapacitated or under extreme duress, unleashing his raw, unbridled psychic nature. Throughout his journey, Mob transitions from a boy who fears his own heart to a young man who accepts his powers as a part of his identity, ultimately realizing that his true strength lies not in his telekinesis, but in his unwavering kindness and capacity for empathy.	https://mob-psycho-100.fandom.com/wiki/Shigeo_Kageyama
