Orochimaru	{https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/naruto/images/1/14/Orochimaru_Infobox.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/1000?cb=20150925223113,https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/naruto/images/6/6f/Orochimaru_As_A_Kid.PNG/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/1000?cb=20210915212747,https://scontent-iad3-1.xx.fbcdn.net/v/t39.30808-6/302304895_590737335841273_3241175021445052459_n.jpg?_nc_cat=110&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=6ee11a&_nc_ohc=wBdVDF27x6YQ7kNvwHTevYJ&_nc_oc=Adn29-23GB2mgng3XRSc0DJZdG7Lj8eu-cdi_JTrxJ014LS8oZfQ3LqFzPaxylzuMz0nlhXXXn2xVrXRCCORdRO7&_nc_zt=23&_nc_ht=scontent-iad3-1.xx&_nc_gid=2IGBS-PcpqG87dcAVUHewA&oh=00_AfgLZgli1On6y-MXxueSz28g7EuUxmf6-Esa5MggSeOZsQ&oe=6921E8F8,https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/33/Orochimaru%2C_Screenshot_%28manga%29.jpg,https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/boruto/images/b/be/Orochimaru_Part_III.png/revision/latest?cb=20170903204503,https://i1.sndcdn.com/artworks-mfGNhE0pSSpL11Wz-sEqZIg-t1080x1080.jpg,https://www.reddit.com/media?url=https%3A%2F%2Fpreview.redd.it%2Fhow-badly-has-orochimaru-been-ruined-as-an-antagonist-v0-kzahgw0x7ocf1.jpeg%3Fauto%3Dwebp%26s%3D749a1d4a7085f14cbe585f0ee4ebab4fe6b631ec,https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/villains/images/5/5a/Orochimaru.png/revision/latest?cb=20220618055421,https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/33/Orochimaru%2C_Screenshot_%28manga%29.jpg}	Naruto	35	Orochimaru is one of the "Legendary Sannin" of Konohagakure, a title earned alongside Jiraiya and Tsunade for their immense power during the Second Great Ninja War. Originally a star pupil of the Third Hokage, Orochimaru's path darkened after the death of his parents, which sparked a nihilistic obsession with the fragility of life. Driven by a desire to learn every jutsu in existenceΓÇöa feat impossible in a single human lifespanΓÇöhe turned to unethical human experimentation to achieve immortality. This eventually led to his defection from the village, the founding of his own Hidden Sound Village, and a long-running campaign of terror that included the assassination of his former mentor and the manipulation of Sasuke Uchiha, whom he sought to claim as his next host body.\n\nIn the later years of the series and into the Boruto era, OrochimaruΓÇÖs role shifts from a primary antagonist to a more complex, neutral observer. After being revived during the Fourth Shinobi World War, he realized that his previous attempts to force "change" through destruction were limited, opting instead to watch how Sasuke and the next generation would shape the world. While he remains under constant surveillance by the Hidden Leaf, he has largely abandoned his overtly villainous ambitions in favor of scientific progress, even creating his "son" Mitsuki through advanced cloning. Despite this apparent reformation, he remains a chilling and enigmatic figure, a master of survival who has effectively cheated death and continues to operate from the shadows as a brilliant, if morally gray, scientist.	https://naruto.fandom.com/wiki/Orochimaru
Edward Elrich	{https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/fma/images/b/b4/EdwardManga.png/revision/latest?cb=20250220063707,https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/fma/images/b/bc/Edward09.png/revision/latest?cb=20201016012253,https://static.wikitide.net/greatcharacterswiki/thumb/0/05/Ed_prof.png/800px-Ed_prof.png,https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/fma/images/b/bc/Edward09.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/1000?cb=20201016012253,https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/fma/images/a/a5/Chapter81.jpg/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/1000?cb=20100413133900,https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/fma/images/d/d1/Years.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/1000?cb=20170712012915,https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b5/Edward85as.JPG}	Full Metal Alchemist	36	Edward Elric, famously known as the "Fullmetal Alchemist," is a prodigious alchemist and the youngest State Alchemist in the history of the country of Amestris. His life was permanently altered after a failed attempt to perform the forbidden art of human transmutation to resurrect his deceased mother. This catastrophic event resulted in the loss of his left leg and his younger brother Alphonse's entire body; in a desperate act of sacrifice, Edward gave up his right arm to bind Alphonse's soul to a suit of armor. Now equipped with high-tech "automail" prosthetic limbs, Edward serves the military to gain access to vast resources, driven by a singular, selfless goal: to find the legendary Philosopher's Stone and restore his brother's body.\n\nCharacterized by his golden hair, small stature, and a notoriously short fuseΓÇöespecially when mocked for his heightΓÇöEdward is a brilliant tactical thinker and a formidable martial artist. Unlike many of his peers, he can perform alchemy without the use of a transmutation circle, a rare ability gained from his encounter with the metaphysical being known as "Truth." Despite his cynical view of religion and authority, he possesses a deep sense of justice and adheres strictly to the law of "Equivalent Exchange," believing that science and hard work are the only true paths to salvation. Over the course of his journey, he evolves from a headstrong and guilt-ridden youth into a mature leader who prioritizes the value of human life and the strength of the bonds he shares with his friends and family.\n\nWith his missing limbs replaced by high-tech metal prosthetics called automail, Edward joins the State Military under the command of Colonel Roy Mustang, using the military's resources to search extensively for the legendary Philosopher's Stone.	https://fma.fandom.com/wiki/Edward_Elric
Hiei	{https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/yuyuhakusho/images/3/38/Hiei_%282018_OVA%29_1.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/1000?cb=20230707051533,https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/yuyuhakusho/images/b/bf/Hiei_portrait_YYH_001.png/revision/latest?cb=20230912190836,https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/yuyuhakusho/images/d/d3/Vlcsnap-2011-02-19-11h54m02s241.png/revision/latest?cb=20230612062426,https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/goldbattles/images/5/5b/HieiOfficial.png/revision/latest?cb=20190723195007,https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/p__/images/0/0f/Yu_Yu_Hakusho_-_Hiei_Render.png/revision/latest?cb=20240228040522&path-prefix=protagonist,https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/81/Hiei_%28YuYu_Hakusho%29.png,https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/3c/YuYu_Hakusho_characters.png}	YuYu Hakusho	68	Hiei , also known as Jaganshi Hiei , is a main character in the anime and manga series YuYu Hakusho by Yoshihiro Togashi. He is called "Hiei of the Evil Eye" in the Viz manga. Originally an antagonist during the Spirit Detective Saga, he almost kills Yusuke Urameshi but later becomes one of the four protagonists.	https://yuyuhakusho.fandom.com/wiki/Hiei
Alphonse Elrich	{https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/7c/AlphonseElricArakawa.jpg,https://imgix.ranker.com/list_img_v2/8363/2728363/original/best-alphonse-elric-quotes,"data:image/jpeg;base64,",https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/fma/images/9/9c/AlHuman03.png/revision/latest?cb=20250127205004,https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/fma/images/f/fc/Alphonse_Full_Body.png/revision/latest?cb=20250220120923,https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/fma/images/1/11/Vlcsnap-2010-10-11-08h37m16s176.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/1000?cb=20101011004216,https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/fma/images/e/e1/Fmavol8.jpg/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/1000?cb=20111108213305,https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/fullmetal-alchemist-database/images/f/f6/AlphonseElricEp7.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/1000?cb=20121007031424}	Full Metal Alchemist	37	Alphonse Elric is the younger brother of Edward Elric and a central protagonist in the Fullmetal Alchemist series. During the brothers' ill-fated attempt to bring their mother back to life through human transmutation, Alphonse lost his entire physical body to the "Truth." He only survived because Edward managed to bind his soul to a massive, hollow suit of steel armor using a blood seal. Despite his intimidating, metallic appearance, Alphonse is the emotional heart of the duoΓÇökind-hearted, polite, and often the voice of reason when EdwardΓÇÖs temper flares. His journey is defined by a quiet but profound existential struggle, as he grapples with the sensory deprivation of being a soul without a body, unable to feel warmth, eat, or sleep.\n\nAs the brothers travel across Amestris in search of the Philosopher's Stone, Alphonse develops into a master alchemist and a powerful hand-to-hand combatant. Because his soul was present at the "Gate of Truth," he eventually gains the ability to perform alchemy without a transmutation circle, just like his brother. While Edward is driven by the guilt of what happened to Al, Alphonse remains remarkably selfless, often putting his own restoration on the line to save others. His character arc concludes with a powerful testament to the show's themes of sacrifice and brotherhood, as he eventually learns that the strength of his soul is not defined by the armor that contains it, but by his unwavering compassion and the memories he shares with those he loves.	https://fma.fandom.com/wiki/Alphonse_Elric
Rock Lee	{https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/naruto/images/9/9d/Lee_Pose.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/1000?cb=20150124171221,https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/9e/RockLee.png,https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/94/LeeGateOpen.jpg,https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/disneythehunchbackofnotredame/images/a/a5/Naruto_Episode100-63.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20141210191125,https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/naruto/images/d/db/Drunken_Fist.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/1000?cb=20150124172754,https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/naruto/images/9/9c/Front_Lotus_Lee.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/1000?cb=20240901230614}	Naruto	78	Rock Lee is a dedicated shinobi of the Hidden Leaf VillageΓÇÖs Lee clan and a prominent member of Team Guy, alongside Neji Hy┼½ga and Tenten. Unlike the vast majority of his peers, Lee was born without the ability to use ninjutsu or genjutsu, the traditional energy-based techniques used by ninja. Initially mocked by his classmates for this deficit, he dedicated himself entirely to taijutsu (hand-to-hand combat). Under the mentorship of Might Guy, who saw his own youthful struggles reflected in the boy, Lee transformed himself into a martial arts master. His character is defined by his unwavering optimism, his signature green jumpsuit and bowl cut, and his "ninja way": to prove that a "dropout" can surpass a natural genius through sheer hard work and perseverance.\n\nThroughout the series, Lee is known for pushing his body to extreme physical limits, often using the Eight GatesΓÇöa forbidden technique that unlocks the body's internal limiters to grant explosive power at the cost of physical health. One of his most iconic moments occurred during the Ch┼½nin Exams, where he removed his heavy training weights to reveal staggering speed in a legendary battle against Gaara. Despite suffering injuries that nearly ended his career as a shinobi, his resolve allowed him to undergo a successful but risky operation and return to duty. In his later years, Lee achieved the rank of J┼ìnin and continued his legacy by training his son, Metal Lee, in the same rigorous style of martial arts.	https://naruto.fandom.com/wiki/Rock_Lee
Might Guy	{https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/naruto/images/3/31/Might_Guy.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/1000?cb=20150401084456,https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/naruto/images/b/b3/Might_Guy_Part_III.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/1000?cb=20180824080931,https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/naruto/images/6/64/Kid_Might_Guy.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/1000?cb=20150702114648,https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/naruto/images/1/10/Team_Gai.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/1000?cb=20160303083320,https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/naruto/images/2/26/Guy%27s_Eight_Inner_Gates.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/1000?cb=20150709142413,https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/naruto/images/2/25/Guy_summons_Ningame_Midair.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/1000?cb=20120218214716,https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/naruto/images/4/46/Strong_Fist.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/1000?cb=20150129145542}	Naruto	79	Might Guy is a high-ranking J┼ìnin of the Hidden Leaf Village and the eccentric leader of Team Guy. Born the son of Might Duy, known as the "Eternal Genin," Guy grew up with a significant disadvantage as he lacked natural talent in ninjutsu and genjutsu. Despite being underestimated and mocked for his bowl cut and green jumpsuit, he dedicated himself to mastering taijutsu (hand-to-hand combat) through grueling training and an indomitable spirit. He is defined by his "Power of Youth" philosophy, a radiant optimism he uses to encourage his star pupil, Rock Lee, and his self-proclaimed rival, Kakashi Hatake.\n\nIn battle, Guy is recognized as one of the world's most formidable martial artists, capable of opening the Eight Inner Gates to bypass the bodyΓÇÖs physical limits. By opening these gates, he gains astronomical speed and power, culminating in techniques like the "Morning Peacock" and "Daytime Tiger." His strength reached its peak during the Fourth Shinobi World War when he opened the final Gate of Death to face Madara Uchiha, a feat so impressive it earned him praise as the strongest taijutsu user in history. Though the toll of his final battle left him permanently wheelchair-bound, Guy remains a symbol of how sheer perseverance can overcome the absence of innate talent.	https://naruto.fandom.com/wiki/Might_Guy
Neji Hyuga	{https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/naruto/images/7/7e/Neji_Part_I.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/1000?cb=20160118081119,https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/naruto/images/a/a8/Neji_Part_II.png/revision/latest?cb=20150710102654,https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/naruto/images/a/aa/Neji_cursemark.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/1000?cb=20150128190233,https://static0.srcdn.com/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/Hiashi-Hyuga-Apologizes-To-Neji-After-The-Chunin-Exams-In-Naruto.jpg,https://static0.srcdn.com/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/Tenten-Saves-Neji-From-Spicy-Curry-In-Naruto.jpg,https://static0.srcdn.com/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/Neji-Sacrifices-Himself-For-Hinata-And-Naruto-In-The-Fourth-Shinobi-World-War.jpg,https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ninja-alliance/images/9/96/Byakugan.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20130709003804}	Naruto	80	Neji Hy┼½ga was a prodigy of the Hidden Leaf Village's noble Hy┼½ga clan and a member of Team Guy. Despite his immense natural talent and mastery of the Byakugan and the Gentle Fist fighting style, Neji was born into the clan's Branch House. This meant he was marked with a "Caged Bird" seal on his forehead, a curse intended to bind him to a life of service to the Main House and ensure his powerful eyes could never be stolen. This systemic oppression fueled a deep-seated fatalism in Neji; he grew up believing that a personΓÇÖs destiny was predetermined at birth and that no amount of effort could change one's fixed path in life.\n\nEverything changed for Neji during the Ch┼½nin Exams after his defeat at the hands of Naruto Uzumaki. NarutoΓÇÖs refusal to give up, despite being labeled a "failure," shattered NejiΓÇÖs rigid worldview and taught him that destiny is something one carves for themselves. Following this revelation, Neji transformed from a cold, arrogant antagonist into a compassionate and protective teammate. He spent the rest of his life striving to be truly free, eventually becoming a J┼ìnin and a mentor to his cousin Hinata. He ultimately fulfilled his self-chosen destiny during the Fourth Shinobi World War, sacrificing his life to protect Naruto and Hinata, proving that his final act was a choice made out of love rather than an obligation of his birth.	https://naruto.fandom.com/wiki/Neji_Hy%C5%ABga
Utena Tenjou	{https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/utena/images/8/86/Ba%C5%9Fl%C4%B1ks%C4%B1z2141_20250819184426.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/1000?cb=20250819154724,https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/utena/images/5/56/B.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20170822031259,https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/utena/images/3/30/E.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20170822031907,https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/utena/images/1/16/Utena.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20110629191601,https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/utena/images/8/8f/Series_ep09_070.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20160105093544,https://davedalessiowrites.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/09/utena-tenjou.jpg?w=640,https://a.storyblok.com/f/178900/640x478/94459cce42/ad2d7699e17b79616cb80206076b48bb1576637232_full.png/m/640x478}	Revolutionary Girl Utena 	81	Utena Tenjou is the spirited and unconventional protagonist of the series, defined by her unwavering desire to become a "prince." After losing her parents as a young child, she was consoled by a mysterious traveling prince who gave her a rose-engraved signet ring and promised they would meet again. Deeply moved by his nobility and compassion, Utena vowed to eschew the traditional role of a princess and instead embody the strength and chivalry of the prince she admired. At Ohtori Academy, she famously defies the school's strict dress code by wearing a modified male uniform, a Choice that contributes to her immense popularity among her female peers. Athletic, forthright, and fiercely protective, Utena is driven by a simple but powerful sense of justice that often borders on naivety.\n\nHer life takes a surreal turn when she is drawn into a series of ritualistic sword duels in the forest behind the academy. Initially motivated by a desire to defend her friend WakabaΓÇÖs honor from the arrogant Kyouichi Saionji, Utena unintentionally wins the "Rose Bride," Anthy Himemiya. As she becomes Anthy's protector and "fianc├⌐e," Utena is forced to navigate a complex web of manipulation and psychological trauma orchestrated by the Student Council and the mysterious "End of the World." Throughout the series, UtenaΓÇÖs journey evolves from a childhood fantasy of heroism into a more profound quest for self-actualization. She ultimately strives to break the metaphorical "shell of the world" to find a true sense of agency for both herself and Anthy, redefining what it truly means to be noble in a world filled with artifice.	https://utena.fandom.com/wiki/Utena_Tenjou
\.
